Nrityapath AI

AI-powered Bharatanatyam movement & storytelling notation generator

Nrityapath uses AI to convert movement descriptions or narrative stories into structured Bharatanatyam choreography notation — complete with posture glyphs, mudras, beats, expression cues, and teaching notes.

It introduces a new, lightweight digital notation standard for classical Indian dance:
NNF — Nrityapath Notation Format

⸻

What Is Nrityapath?

Bharatanatyam has been passed down for centuries orally, visually, and physically — but never through a modern digital notation system.

Nrityapath bridges that gap.

Using AI, it transforms natural language into clear, structured choreography sequences suitable for:
	•	learning
	•	teaching
	•	documenting
	•	choreographing
	•	storytelling
	•	preservation & archiving

It operates in two modes:

Movement → Notation

Short phrases describing posture, mudra, direction, and beats.

Story → Notation

Narratives describing characters, scenarios, or emotional expressions.

Both modes output standardized JSON following the NNF schema.

⸻

Who Is It For?

Primary Users
	•	Dancers (beginner ↔ advanced)
	•	Choreographers
	•	Students learning adavus / abhinaya

Secondary Users
	•	Teachers / Gurus
	•	Movement storytellers
	•	Designers & developers exploring classical arts + AI
	•	Anyone who learns visually or structurally

⸻

Key Features

✔ Text → Structured Dance Notation

Convert phrases or adavus into step-by-step NNF instructions.

✔ Story → Choreography

Translate rasa-based narratives into expressive dance sequences.

✔ NNF Schema

Complete with:
	•	posture codes (ARA, SAM, MND)
	•	hand mudras (ALA, KAT, TRI, PTA)
	•	movements (FWD, TURN_R, STATIC…)
	•	beats (1B, 2B, 4B)
	•	direction codes
	•	rasa expression
	•	teaching notes

✔ Visual Renderer (Framer UI)

Each step can be displayed as:
	•	stick figure posture
	•	mudra icon
	•	direction arrow
	•	beat timing
	•	rasa cues
	•	teaching note

✔ Designed for AI Genesis Hackathon

Built to integrate seamlessly with:
	•	Gemini (prompting & generation)
	•	Opus (workflow automation, review, audit)
	•	Framer (UI visualization)

⸻

NNF — Nrityapath Notation Format

Full specification lives here:
nnf_schema.md

Simplified Output Structure

{
  "mode": "movement",
  "level": "beginner",
  "rasa": "none",
  "steps": [
      { /* step object */ }
  ]
}

